# Testing Architecture Components

ViewModels and repositories are unit-tested with fakes or Mockito. Do not hit the network or a real Room file in local unit tests.

```kotlin
// ❌ BAD — no InstantTaskExecutorRule; real repository; LiveData never observed
class SearchViewModelTest {
    @Test fun basic() {
        SearchViewModel(RepoRepository()).setQuery("foo")
    }
}

// ✅ GOOD — sync executor, mock collaborator, observeForever, verify interactions
@RunWith(JUnit4::class)
class SearchViewModelTest {
    @Rule @JvmField val instantExecutor = InstantTaskExecutorRule()
    private val repository = mock(RepoRepository::class.java)

    @Test fun basic() {
        val viewModel = SearchViewModel(repository)
        viewModel.results.observeForever(mock())
        viewModel.setQuery("foo")
        verify(repository).search("foo")
    }
}
```

- Use `InstantTaskExecutorRule` whenever tests read `LiveData`.
- Coroutine LiveData tests use a `MainCoroutineRule` / test dispatcher and helpers like `getOrAwaitValue` (`LiveDataSample`).
- `GithubBrowserSample`: mock ViewModels in Espresso fragment tests; use MockWebServer for Retrofit; in-memory Room for DAO tests on device.
- Prefer fakes over mocks for data sources you own (`FakeDataSource` in `LiveDataSample`).
- New production behavior needs tests in the same sample; run that sample's Gradle test tasks, not an invented repo-wide suite unless using `run_all_tests.sh`.
